// that was lost. An empty table lets the file load cleanly with no CA data, which is strictly better
// than a hard error -- but the CA tree WILL be empty until this is implemented for real.
//
// Doing it properly means reading CharacterAdvancement.dbc and emitting one table per row with the
// fields the Lua reads: ID, Class, Tab, Flags, Spells, Type, ParentNode, Distance, Color, Anchor,
// NodeType, DraftRequired_XOR, RequiredIDs, PositionX/Y, Masteries. The column mapping is only
// partly known (spell chain [5..9], level [28], class type [32]); the rest should come from the
// decompiled serializer FUN_10172df0, which is what the real binding uses to build this table.
// Guessing the indices would produce a plausible but wrong talent tree, so it is left undone.
static int Asc_CA_GetAllEntries(lua_State* L)
{
    return ::AscCA_GetAllEntries(L);
}

